{
  "id": "710kyqc",
  "title": "Chapter 10: Acids, Bases and Salts",
  "order": 59,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qemrzrn",
      "content": "Acids, bases and salts are important classes of chemical compounds that play a crucial role in chemistry and daily life. These substances participate in numerous chemical reactions and are widely used in industries, laboratories and households."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "pH Range",
          "value": "0 to 14",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Neutral pH",
          "value": "7.0",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Acidic pH",
          "value": "< 7.0",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Basic pH",
          "value": "> 7.0",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "xb5bn4j"
    },
    {
      "id": "2oclcul",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Acids"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Acids release hydrogen ions (H+) in aqueous solutions, taste sour, and turn blue litmus paper red.",
        "Bases release hydroxide ions (OH-) in water, taste bitter, feel soapy, and turn red litmus paper blue.",
        "Alkalis are bases that dissolve completely in water, such as Sodium Hydroxide (NaOH) and Potassium Hydroxide (KOH).",
        "The pH scale measures the hydrogen ion concentration, ranging from 0 (strongly acidic) to 14 (strongly alkaline).",
        "A neutralization reaction occurs between an acid and a base to produce a salt and water."
      ],
      "id": "t3mc5tb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cgrz6eu",
      "content": "• Acids are substances that produce hydrogen ions (H⁺) when dissolved in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "77ow3c8",
      "content": "• They have a sour taste."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hbqi59d",
      "content": "• They turn blue litmus paper red."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ds6uxfy",
      "content": "• They react with metals to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jszobdv",
      "content": "Examples of common acids:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "t7sxh69",
      "content": "• Hydrochloric acid (HCl)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w9j2yz1",
      "content": "• Sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2fa2fbo",
      "content": "• Nitric acid (HNO₃)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bqb8fp7",
      "content": "• Acetic acid (CH₃COOH)"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7olvx0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Bases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vku5qtr",
      "content": "• Bases are substances that produce hydroxide ions (OH⁻) in aqueous solution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ckf3i8r",
      "content": "• They taste bitter and feel slippery."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9lfex51",
      "content": "• They turn red litmus paper blue."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3lm6pa",
      "content": "Examples of bases:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4b17dxt",
      "content": "• Sodium hydroxide (NaOH)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zzeazu6",
      "content": "• Potassium hydroxide (KOH)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qnjn2fn",
      "content": "• Calcium hydroxide Ca(OH)₂"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "A neutralization reaction occurs when an acid reacts with a base to form salt and water.",
      "id": "d69eqod"
    },
    {
      "id": "o28xegl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Alkalis"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sz7anby",
      "content": "Alkalis are bases that dissolve in water and produce hydroxide ions. All alkalis are bases but all bases are not alkalis."
    },
    {
      "id": "blgmuxx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Properties of Acids and Bases"
    },
    {
      "id": "0nlfeqb",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Property</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Acids</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Bases</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Taste</p>",
            "<p>Sour</p>",
            "<p>Bitter</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Litmus test</p>",
            "<p>Blue → Red</p>",
            "<p>Red → Blue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>pH value</p>",
            "<p>Less than 7</p>",
            "<p>Greater than 7</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Reaction with metals</p>",
            "<p>Produces hydrogen gas</p>",
            "<p>Usually no reaction</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "veki3ck",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Strength of Acids and Bases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qkvgkiy",
      "content": "• Strong acids completely ionize in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k1eha13",
      "content": "• Weak acids partially ionize in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tkat3dn",
      "content": "• Strong bases completely ionize in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4lmk75q",
      "content": "• Weak bases partially ionize."
    },
    {
      "id": "ytazzv7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. pH Scale"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3t9blex",
      "content": "The pH scale measures the acidity or basicity of a solution and ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Property",
        "Acids",
        "Bases"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Taste",
          "Sour",
          "Bitter"
        ],
        [
          "Ions Produced in Water",
          "H+ (Hydronium / H3O+)",
          "OH- (Hydroxide)"
        ],
        [
          "Litmus Paper Test",
          "Turns Blue litmus Red",
          "Turns Red litmus Blue"
        ],
        [
          "Phenolphthalein Test",
          "Remains Colorless",
          "Turns Pink"
        ],
        [
          "Texture / Feeling",
          "Corrosive to skin",
          "Slippery or Soapy"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "qj0j0ca"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "acfex1i",
      "content": "pH &lt; 7 : Acidic solution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x9lpx3f",
      "content": "pH = 7 : Neutral solution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xknbdgf",
      "content": "pH &gt; 7 : Basic solution"
    },
    {
      "id": "ju68n0l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Indicators"
    },
    {
