        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g68p1v8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v1m9hqz",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a8aj4hd",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ud3d9ba",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "gizop61",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z33edf5",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qq5mumd",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3xexz4",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Litmus is a natural indicator derived from lichens; phenolphthalein turns pink in basic solutions and colorless in acidic solutions.",
        "Strong acids (e.g., HCl, H2SO4, HNO3) dissociate completely in water, while weak acids (e.g., CH3COOH) dissociate partially.",
        "Important commercial formulas often asked: Baking Soda (NaHCO3), Washing Soda (Na2CO3·10H2O), and Plaster of Paris (CaSO4·1/2H2O).",
        "Rainwater is considered acid rain when its pH drops below 5.6 due to dissolved oxides of nitrogen and sulfur."
      ],
      "id": "q7qiyi0"
    },
    {
      "id": "wbz7sbb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g68ywpz",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ic02k5i",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "af60c6n",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "el6els1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l52bm6x",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ltvpfe7",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5lhmctm",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5swmhbj",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}